`carve` deliberately allocates <= 1 GiB to try to stay inside the reservation;
`gtt`/`man`/`pin` use the requested 48.0 GiB. The vram+/gtt+ columns are sysfs
counters sampled around the allocation, so placement is measured, not assumed.
tok/s cap = read BW / 2.525 GB per decode token (spec 01.7).
